{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#977","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#977","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#977\",\"parent_revision\":\"6be5ab4b687df55621e5f24165db8a075e5e77196ea3e5ecdd203c1e3147a5d2\",\"root_revision\":\"6be5ab4b687df55621e5f24165db8a075e5e77196ea3e5ecdd203c1e3147a5d2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe built-in /simplify skill only reviews source code (redundant state, copy-paste, N+1 queries, JSX nesting). It skips markdown, YAML, skill files, agent definitions, and plan artifacts. Sessions that produce only planning artifacts, documentation, or skill edits get no quality review. A custom /simplify-all (or replacement) skill should also check for: duplicate content across markdown files, stale cross-references and broken links, inconsistent formatting, invalid documentation claims, redundant instructions across skills/agents, and plan artifact quality (missing sections, incomplete acceptance criteria).\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Built-in /simplify skill scope limitation | AVAILABLE | Item description confirms code-only coverage |\\n| 2 | Plugin location for new skill | AVAILABLE | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/` or standalone plugin |\\n| 3 | Broken link detection tool | AVAILABLE | `uv run prek run` + markdown-link-check |\\n| 4 | Duplicate content detection approach | MISSING | Algorithm not defined |\\n\\nVerdict: READY with one algorithm design decision (duplicate content detection).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Medium complexity. Additive skill. No code modifications. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A `/simplify-all` skill (or replacement for `/simplify`) reviews: markdown files for duplicate content and stale cross-references, YAML files for inconsistent formatting, skill/agent definitions for redundant instructions, plan artifacts for missing sections and incomplete acceptance criteria\\n- Checks include: duplicate content across markdown files, broken links, invalid documentation claims, redundant instructions across skills/agents\\n- Skill produces a structured report: file, issue type, suggested fix\\n- Invocable as `/simplify-all` with optional `--files <pattern>` to scope to specific file types\\n- Skill does not modify files \u2014 report only; user decides what to fix\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/simplify-all/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill (or extend existing simplify skill)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/simplify-all/scripts/` \u2014 supporting scripts if needed\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer whose session produces only planning artifacts, documentation, or skill edits, I need a `/simplify-all` skill that reviews all changed file types (not just code) so I get quality feedback on markdown, YAML, skill files, and plan artifacts too.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **create a broad simplify skill that reviews all changed file types, not just code** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-03-21 \u2014 /simplify ran on a planning-only session and found nothing to review\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ba8b8639694f7e3ccb93dce250895608f2d628b11e216974ca579f03a62f2368\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTE8Iw\"}"}